    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `initials` field on the owner API response.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and it's documented in the API contract.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped the new field via a MapStruct expression, mirroring the existing `displayName` pattern:\n   - `formatInitials(owner)` composes the two initials.\n   - a small private `initial(name)` helper returns the upper-cased first letter plus a dot \u2014 single responsibility, reused for both names.\n\nThis keeps the name-formatting/presentation logic colocated with `formatDisplayName` in the mapper rather than scattering it, and reuses the same computed-DTO-field convention already established.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComputesInitials` (`john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.`) and the full test suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS, 0 failures).",
